    "description": "NextDecade develops LNG export infrastructure and associated carbon capture projects centered on the Rio Grande LNG complex in South Texas. Its customer base includes global LNG buyers, project-finance lenders, and industrial or utility counterparties entering long-term sales and capacity arrangements, and the company follows an asset-heavy development model built around long-term contracted liquefaction trains. The business is concentrated in Brownsville, Texas, where it is developing a multi-train LNG export facility with associated pipeline interconnections and carbon capture plans. Public disclosures describe Phase 1 as 27 million tonnes per annum of liquefaction capacity across the first three trains, with later trains under development and financing. Global Infrastructure Partners agreed to invest in Rio Grande LNG Phase 1 in July 2023, and Mubadala has also been disclosed as an investor in NextDecade-related capital raises and project commitments. In October 2025, NextDecade announced a positive final investment decision on Train 5, further expanding the project.",
